  "row_count": 18,
  "notes": {
    "raw": "Phase changes: 505.12 K, melting point of Sn; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 1.680$ kcal/mol. \n875 K, $\\alpha - \\beta$ transition point of SnS; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 0.120$ kcal/mol. \n1153 K, melting point of SnS; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 7.530$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n<table><tr><td>298.15-875 K:</td><td> $Cp^o$  = 8.066 + 8.254 $x10^{-3}T$  + 1.105 $x10^5T^{-2}$ </td></tr><tr><td>875-1153 K:</td><td> $H^o-H_{298}^o$  = 8.066 $x10^{-3}T$  + 4.127 $x10^{-6}T^2$  - 1.105 $x10^2T^{-1}$  - 2.401 $Cp^o$  = 8.429 + 5.132 $x10^{-3}T$ </td></tr><tr><td>1153-1300 K:</td><td> $H^o-H_{298}^o$  = 8.429 $x10^{-3}T$  + 2.566 $x10^{-6}T^2$  - 1.530 $Cp^o$  = 18.000</td></tr><tr><td></td><td> $H^o-H_{298}^o$  = 18.000 $x10^{-3}T$  - 1.624</td></tr></table>\nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-505.12 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -40.720 - 1.074 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} + 1.625 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} - 137.050 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -40.720 + 1.074 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln T - 1.625 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} - 68.525 \\text{T}^{-1} + 14.097 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">505.12-875 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -42.685 - 2.296 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} + 3.786 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 40.750 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -42.685 + 2.296 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln T - 3.786 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 20.375 \\text{T}^{-1} + 11.119 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">875-1153 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -41.814 - 1.934 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} + 2.225 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 151.250 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -41.814 + 1.934 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln T - 2.225 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 75.625 \\text{T}^{-1} + 11.144 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">1153-1300 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -41.908 + 7.637 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} - 0.341 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 151.250 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -41.908 - 7.637 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln T + 0.341 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 75.625 \\text{T}^{-1} + 75.744 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr></table>\nSources: Enthalpy of formation at 298 K from Mills (80). Low-temperature heat capacities and entropy at 298 K from King (65). High-temperature data based on Orr (89). ",
    "lines_raw": [
